INV-rahib Surface 1. `_pre_scenario_b_gate` stops the timeout and hung-run
paths from closing-and-repushing a PR that already merged or is about to.
Its second sub-case read `mergeable` through `json_field`, which prints the
empty string for a JSON null exactly as it does for a missing key -- so
`mergeable: null` was indistinguishable from `false` and the gate silently
ordered the close.

GitHub computes mergeability asynchronously and reports null until that
background job finishes, i.e. null is the expected value in the seconds
after a push, which is exactly when this gate fires. The sub-case was
therefore inert on the live backend for as long as it existed, and the
PR-churn cycle it exists to prevent is the one WI-buniz was downstream of.

- json_bool_state reads a JSON boolean as a tri-state (true/false/null/
  absent/other/unreadable). Unknown mergeability re-queries /pulls/<n> once,
  then defers to a green CI rather than destroying a PR on an unread field.
  false, absent and unreadable still fall through to the close.
- Measured against the pre-fix library in both directions: null 1 -> 0,
  true 0 -> 0, false 1 -> 1. Exactly one cell moves; `false` holding is the
  control that this is not a blanket "never close".
- ci-debug pr-status now prints `Mergeable:` as a tri-state. It was
  unobservable through any approved script, which is why this went
  unverified against the real backend for as long as it did.
- The 19 existing tests fed the gate only true/false, and one asserted the
  literal source line the fix had to change -- so it broke exactly when the
  bug was fixed and pointed the fixer at keeping it. Loosened to the
  dependency it was really guarding.

Refines the invariant, which was unsatisfiable as written (owner ruling
2026-08-03): it demanded "no third state" while auto-pr has 20 terminal
states, three of them deliberate non-merge outcomes -- queued_vpr (the vPR
queue was re-affirmed under WI-hajif Ruling 2), governance_pending and
noop_empty_queue. Replaced by a declared closed set with `unknown` as the
violation signal, enforced in both directions: no emitted state undeclared,
no declared state unreachable, plus a non-vacuity floor.

Adds .git/AUTOPR_HISTORY.jsonl, because the invariant had no instrument.
AUTOPR_LAST_RESULT.json is overwritten every run -- correct for WI-miriz's
"did my backgrounded run succeed?" sentinel, and pinned by its own test --
so the 2026-06-17 validation criterion had nothing to evaluate and went
unexamined across 579 commits. Convergence is a property of the sequence of
runs, so it gets its own append-only artifact rather than a second meaning
bolted onto the sentinel. Best-effort: an observability artifact must never
turn a successful run into a failed one.

Governance files touched with explicit human approval (auto-pr, ci-debug,
lib/forgejo-api.sh), approved without --gov.

